To avoid any confusion, this is bit true.  Any sampler that is working should be exploring the entire parameter space with reasonable probability mass (what we call the typical set).

What is true is that algorithms like Random Walk Metropolis and the Gibbs sampler often break (without any obvious indication) and don't explore everything.

> Unlike the other samplers Stan does try to explore the full parameter space

